WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:17.761
For the past few years,
we've been calling men out.

00:00:19.103 --> 00:00:20.302
It had to be done.

00:00:20.326 --> 00:00:22.278
(Applause)

00:00:22.302 --> 00:00:27.646
But lately, I've been thinking
we need to do something even harder.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:32.149
We need, as my good friend
Tony Porter says,

00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:35.889
to find a way to call men in.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:41.420
My father began to sexually abuse me
when I was five years old.

00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:45.681
He would come into my room
in the middle of the night.

00:00:45.705 --> 00:00:47.515
He appeared to be in a trance.

00:00:48.476 --> 00:00:51.150
The abuse continued until I was 10.

00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:54.149
When I tried to resist him,

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:56.960
when I was finally able to say no,

00:00:56.984 --> 00:00:58.792
he began to beat me.

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:00.590
He called me stupid.

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:01.974
He said I was a liar.

00:01:02.974 --> 00:01:05.705
The sexual abuse ended when I was 10,

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:08.562
but actually, it never ended.

00:01:09.531 --> 00:01:11.237
It changed who I was.

00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:16.298
I was filled with anxiety and guilt
and shame all the time,

00:01:16.322 --> 00:01:18.121
and I didn't know why.

00:01:18.145 --> 00:01:21.200
I hated my body, I hated myself,

00:01:21.224 --> 00:01:22.970
I got sick a lot,

00:01:22.994 --> 00:01:24.300
I couldn't think,

00:01:24.324 --> 00:01:25.946
I couldn't remember things.

00:01:26.343 --> 00:01:29.545
I was drawn to dangerous men and women

00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:34.438
who I allowed -- actually, I invited --
to treat me badly,

00:01:34.462 --> 00:01:37.276
because that is what my father
taught me love was.

00:01:38.708 --> 00:01:43.237
I waited my whole life
for my father to apologize to me.

00:01:44.118 --> 00:01:45.470
He didn't.

00:01:45.494 --> 00:01:47.009
He wouldn't.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.794
And then, with the recent
scandals of famous men,

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:53.207
as one after another was exposed,

00:01:53.231 --> 00:01:54.381
I realized something:

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:58.536
I have never heard a man

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.758
who has committed rape
or physical violence

00:02:02.782 --> 00:02:06.838
ever publicly apologize to his victim.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.116
I began to wonder,

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:15.360
what would an authentic,
deep apology be like?

00:02:20.179 --> 00:02:23.702
So, something strange began to happen.

00:02:24.404 --> 00:02:26.282
I began to write,

00:02:26.306 --> 00:02:29.290
and my father's voice
began to come through me.

00:02:30.235 --> 00:02:32.782
He began to tell me what he had done

00:02:32.806 --> 00:02:34.245
and why.

00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:37.104
He began to apologize.

00:02:37.128 --> 00:02:39.589
My father is dead almost 31 years,

00:02:39.613 --> 00:02:41.361
and yet, in this apology,

00:02:41.385 --> 00:02:43.977
the one I had to write for him,

00:02:44.001 --> 00:02:48.486
I discovered the power of an apology

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.241
and how it actually might be
the way to move forward

00:02:51.265 --> 00:02:53.364
in the crisis we now face

00:02:53.388 --> 00:02:56.414
with men and all the women they abuse.

00:02:57.196 --> 00:03:00.966
Apology is a sacred commitment.

00:03:01.798 --> 00:03:04.061
It requires complete honesty.

00:03:04.719 --> 00:03:07.948
It demands deep
self-interrogation and time.

00:03:07.972 --> 00:03:09.671
It cannot be rushed.

00:03:10.052 --> 00:03:13.140
I discovered an apology has four steps,

00:03:13.164 --> 00:03:16.133
and, if you would,
I'd like to take you through them.

00:03:16.157 --> 00:03:19.989
The first is you have to say
what, in detail, you did.

00:03:20.858 --> 00:03:22.807
Your accounting cannot be vague.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.682
"I'm sorry if I hurt you"

00:03:24.706 --> 00:03:26.707
or "I'm sorry if I sexually abused you"

00:03:26.731 --> 00:03:28.049
doesn't cut it.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.474
You have to say what actually happened.

00:03:32.351 --> 00:03:34.676
"I came into the room
in the middle of the night,

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.074
and I pulled your underpants down."

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.921
"I belittled you because
I was jealous of you

00:03:39.945 --> 00:03:42.349
and I wanted you to feel less."

00:03:42.373 --> 00:03:45.358
The liberation is in the details.

00:03:46.088 --> 00:03:48.930
An apology is a remembering.

00:03:48.954 --> 00:03:51.426
It connects the past with the present.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.712
It says that what occurred
actually did occur.

00:03:55.838 --> 00:04:00.203
The second step
is you have to ask yourself why.

00:04:00.997 --> 00:04:04.019
Survivors are haunted by the why.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:09.139
Why? Why would my father want
to sexually abuse his eldest daughter?

00:04:09.163 --> 00:04:12.535
Why would he take my head
and smash it against a wall?

00:04:15.565 --> 00:04:17.668
In my father's case,

00:04:17.692 --> 00:04:21.666
he was a child born long after
the other children.

00:04:22.671 --> 00:04:26.020
He was an accident
that became "the miracle."

00:04:26.495 --> 00:04:30.090
He was adored and treated
as the golden boy.

00:04:30.714 --> 00:04:33.774
But adoration, it turns out, is not love.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.863
Adoration is a projection

00:04:35.887 --> 00:04:38.157
of someone's need for you to be perfect

00:04:38.181 --> 00:04:39.331
onto you.

00:04:39.788 --> 00:04:42.731
My father had to live up
to this impossible ideal,

00:04:42.755 --> 00:04:45.029
and so he was never allowed to be himself.

00:04:45.441 --> 00:04:47.502
He was never allowed to express tenderness

00:04:47.526 --> 00:04:50.759
or vulnerability, curiosity, doubt.

00:04:50.783 --> 00:04:52.999
He was never allowed to cry.

00:04:53.023 --> 00:04:56.187
And so he was forced to push
all those feelings underground,

00:04:56.211 --> 00:04:59.100
and they eventually metastasized.

00:04:59.124 --> 00:05:03.295
Those suppressed feelings
later became Shadowman,

00:05:03.319 --> 00:05:04.963
and he was out of control,

00:05:04.987 --> 00:05:08.549
and he eventually unleashed
his torrent on me.

00:05:10.215 --> 00:05:14.215
The third step is you have
to open your heart

00:05:14.239 --> 00:05:18.263
and feel what your victim felt
as you were abusing her.

00:05:19.072 --> 00:05:21.032
You have to let your heart break.

00:05:21.056 --> 00:05:23.204
You have to feel the horror and betrayal

00:05:23.228 --> 00:05:27.270
and the long-term impacts
of your abuse on your victim.

00:05:27.883 --> 00:05:31.167
You have to sit with the suffering
you have caused.

00:05:31.729 --> 00:05:33.373
And, of course, the fourth step

00:05:33.397 --> 00:05:36.594
is taking responsibility
for what you have done

00:05:36.618 --> 00:05:38.529
and making amends.

00:05:38.977 --> 00:05:44.474
So, why would anyone want to go through
such a grueling and humbling process?

00:05:44.982 --> 00:05:47.721
Why would you want to rip yourself open?

00:05:48.636 --> 00:05:52.829
Because it is the only thing
that will set yourself free.

00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:56.540
It is the only thing
that will set your victim free.

00:05:56.564 --> 00:05:59.384
You didn't just destroy your victim.

00:05:59.408 --> 00:06:01.455
You destroyed yourself.

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:05.606
There is no one who enacts
violence on another person

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.495
who doesn't suffer
from the effects themselves.

00:06:09.348 --> 00:06:15.988
It creates an incredibly dark
and contaminating spirit,

00:06:16.012 --> 00:06:18.411
and it spreads
throughout your entire life.

00:06:19.962 --> 00:06:22.732
The apology I wrote -- I learned something

00:06:22.756 --> 00:06:25.156
about a different lens
we have to look through

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.203
to understand the problem
of men's violence

00:06:28.227 --> 00:06:32.121
that I and one billion
other women have survived.

00:06:32.438 --> 00:06:34.600
We often turn to punishment first.

00:06:35.576 --> 00:06:38.000
It's our first instinct, but actually,

00:06:38.024 --> 00:06:42.440
although punishment
sometimes is effective,

00:06:42.464 --> 00:06:44.714
on its own, it is not enough.

00:06:44.738 --> 00:06:46.285
My father punished me.

00:06:46.849 --> 00:06:48.076
I was shut down,

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.051
and I was broken.

00:06:50.587 --> 00:06:54.142
I think punishment hardens us,
but it doesn't teach us.

00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:56.604
Humiliation is not revelation.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:07:02.190
We actually need to create a process
that may involve punishment,

00:07:02.214 --> 00:07:04.529
whereby we open a doorway

00:07:04.553 --> 00:07:09.293
where men can actually become
something and someone else.

00:07:09.847 --> 00:07:12.232
For so many years, I hated my father.

00:07:12.256 --> 00:07:15.234
I wanted him dead. I wanted him in prison.

00:07:15.258 --> 00:07:19.085
But actually, that rage kept me
connected to my father's story.

00:07:20.086 --> 00:07:24.657
What I really wanted
wasn't just for my father to be stopped.

00:07:24.681 --> 00:07:26.253
I wanted him to change.

00:07:26.277 --> 00:07:28.157
I wanted him to apologize.

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.515
That's what we want.

00:07:29.871 --> 00:07:32.172
We don't want men to be destroyed,

00:07:32.196 --> 00:07:34.950
we don't want them to only be punished.

00:07:34.974 --> 00:07:39.632
We want them to see us,
the victims that they have harmed,

00:07:39.656 --> 00:07:41.651
and we want them to repent

00:07:41.675 --> 00:07:43.120
and change.

00:07:43.425 --> 00:07:45.449
And I actually believe this is possible.

00:07:46.474 --> 00:07:49.288
And I really believe it's our way forward.

00:07:49.928 --> 00:07:52.777
But we need men to join us.

00:07:53.354 --> 00:07:58.629
We need men now to be brave
and be part of this transformation.

00:07:59.677 --> 00:08:03.376
I have spent most of my life
calling men out,

00:08:04.344 --> 00:08:06.070
and I am here now,

00:08:07.336 --> 00:08:08.527
right now,

00:08:09.049 --> 00:08:11.517
to call you in.

00:08:13.104 --> 00:08:14.256
Thank you.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.690
(Applause)

00:08:16.714 --> 00:08:17.865
Thank you.

00:08:17.889 --> 00:08:18.905
(Applause)

00:08:18.929 --> 00:08:20.198
Thank you, thank you.

00:08:20.222 --> 00:08:22.317
(Applause)

